  "id": "overcompensation",
  "term": "overcompensation",
  "definition": "Overcompensation is a coping style in schema theory in which a person responds as though the opposite of an underlying schema were true. It is a state-based reaction, involving thoughts, feelings, and behavior aimed at disproving the schema in the moment.",
